<div id="q-ethical-issues" class="question">
  <h3>9. What ethical issues and codes of conduct are there, and how will they be taken into account?</h3>

  <div class="answer">

  {%- if data.dmp.datasets | length > 0 -%}
    {%- if data.dmp.sharedResources.collections | length > 0 -%}
      <p>In our {{ globals.project }}, there {{ 'is' if data.dmp.sharedResources.collections | length == 1 else 'are' }} {{ data.dmp.sharedResources.collections | length }} approach{{ 'es' if data.dmp.sharedResources.collections | length != 1 else '' }} towards ownership, intellectual property rights, and access conditions, as described below:</p>
      <ul>
      {%- for collection in data.dmp.sharedResources.collections -%}
        <li style="margin-bottom: 2em;">

        {{ macros.datasetIntro(collection, "ethical issues", data.dmp.datasets) }}
        {% set numDatasets = collection.usedBy | length %}
        {%- set accessRestriction = collection.accessRestriction -%}

        {# Ethical Legislation #}
        {%- if collection.isSubjectToEthicalReview._value is sameas true -%}
            <p>
            The data collection is subject to ethical legislation.{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.isSubjectToEthicalReview._path) }}
            {%- if collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._value == "not_applicable" %} 
                A new approval or extension of any existing approval under research ethics laws is not applicable for the re-use of the data.{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._path) }}
            {%- elif collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._value == "existing"  %}
                An existing approval under research ethics laws covers our re-use of the data; no new approval or extension is required.{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._path) }}
            {%- elif collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._value == "extension"  %}
                An extension of an existing approval under research ethics laws will be needed for the re-use of the data.{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._path) }}
            {%- elif collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._value == "new"  %}
                A new ethical approval under research ethics laws will be needed to cover our usage of the data.{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.ethicalReview.extensionOfReusedData._path) }}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewLinkDocument or collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewDocument %}
                The protocol from the meeting with the ethics committee is available
                {%- if collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewLinkDocument %}
                    at: <a href="{{ collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewLinkDocument._value }}" target="_blank">{{ collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewLinkDocument._value }}</a>{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewLinkDocument._path) }}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- if collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewDocument %}
                    {%- if collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewLinkDocument %} and can be downloaded {% else %} and can be downloaded {% endif %}
                    <a href="{{ collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewDocument._url}}" target="_blank">here</a>{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.ethicalReview.ethicalReviewDocument._path) }}
                {%- endif %}
                .
            {%- endif -%}
            </p>
        {%- elif collection.isSubjectToEthicalReview._value is sameas false -%}
            <p>The data collection is not subject to ethical legislation.{{ macros.linkQuestion(collection.isSubjectToEthicalReview._path) }}</p>
        {%- else -%}
            <p>No information on ethical aspects were provided.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- else -%}
      <p>No shared resource collections have been defined for this project. Therefore, there are no harmonised ethical issues or codes of conduct to report.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <p>No datasets have been defined for this project. Therefore, there are no ethical issues or codes of conduct to report.</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  {# projects - legislation #}
  {%- set filtered_policies = [] -%}

  {%- for policyItem in data.dmp.policies -%}
    {%- set scope_labels = policyItem.scope | map(attribute='_label') | list -%}
    {%- if 'Ethics and Research Integrity' in scope_labels -%}
      {%- do filtered_policies.append(policyItem) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if filtered_policies | length > 0 -%}
  The following institutional, national, or funder policies and procedures relevant to ethics and research integrity are applicable to {{ globals.project }}:
    <ul>
    {%- for policyItem in filtered_policies -%}
      <li>
        <strong>{{ policyItem.name._value | default("(no name)") }}</strong><br>
        {%- if policyItem.url %} (<a href="{{ policyItem.url._value }}" target="_blank">{{ policyItem.url._value }}</a><br>){%- endif -%}{{ macros.linkQuestion(policyItem.name._path) }}
        {%- if policyItem.description -%}
          <em>{{ policyItem.description._value }}</em><br>
        {%- endif -%}
        Scope: {{ policyItem.scope | map(attribute='_label') | list | join(', ') }}
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  {%- else -%}
    <p>No policies found with scope of ethics and research integrity.</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</div>